Manual review corrections for this page's first pass.

- The two multiple-choice items presenting three candidate equations joined
  the first two equations of each triple inside one math span with a bare
  comma (no space) before breaking out for ", or $...$"; split every
  candidate into its own math span so "or" (and the comma before it) sits
  in plain text between them, matching the pattern already fixed elsewhere
  in this skill's review history.
- "Determine the intersection points of parabolic hyperboloid
  $z=3x^{2}-2y^{2}$..." named the surface backwards: a surface with mixed
  positive/negative quadratic coefficients like this is a hyperbolic
  paraboloid (a saddle), not a "parabolic hyperboloid" (not a standard
  surface name at all); corrected the word order.
- "...reduces to two parallel planes passing." left a dangling trailing
  word with no object, unlike the parallel item above it which ends cleanly
  at "two parallel planes."; removed "passing".
- "(Hint: Find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.)$" trapped the closing sentence
  punctuation ")." inside the math span; moved it outside, matching the
  file's own $z$-axis-style convention of closing math before punctuation.
- "(Hint: Find y from the system consisting of the equations of the
  surfaces.)" left the bound variable y as bare prose although the same
  sentence's surrounding equations and every other single-letter variable
  reference in this file are math-wrapped; changed to $y$.
- "$a=8.7\,\text{mm and}\,c=9.6\,\text{mm}$" and (twice) "$R=2\,\text{and}\,r=1$"
  joined two separate equalities into one math span via \text{and} plus
  manual spacing instead of plain-text "and" between separate math spans,
  the same pattern already flagged and fixed for \text{or} joins in this
  skill's review history; split each into two math spans joined by plain
  "and".
- "The numbers $R$ and $r$ are called are the major and minor radii..."
  duplicated "are"; removed the extra occurrence.

